9359?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jayman2000","html_url":"https://github.com/Jayman2000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jayman2000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jayman2000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jayman2000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jayman2000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jayman2000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jayman2000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jayman2000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jayman2000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jayman2000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-05T19:06:35Z","updated_at":"2024-11-05T19:06:35Z","body":"> Instead, I'll included the hash of the relevant Mozilla commit used by bagder in `thirdparty/README.md`.\r\n\r\nHere’s a tip (since I had to find a bunch of these in order to add the table to the ca-bundle README): the most surefire way to find the hash is to go to [here](https://hg.mozilla.org/releases/mozilla-release/pushloghtml) and then find the push that came right before the timestamp that’s in `ca-certificates.crt`. I had originally tried doing this with `hg log` instead of the pushlog, but it didn’t work well because some commits were made on one date but then pushed to the relevant branch on a later date. The pushlog is the way to go.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2457952635/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2461008989","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98855#issuec